# MyGRACE — Scalable GRACE with Lazy-Loading

This project uses **MyGRACE** (Graph-RAG Anchored Code Engineering) — a scalable variant of GRACE designed for large projects (20-200+ modules).

## Navigation Rule #1 (CRITICAL)
**ALWAYS start with index files. NEVER scan all per-entity files.**

1. Read `docs/graph-index.xml` first (≤100 lines) — find the module ID
2. Read `docs/modules/M-XXX.xml` next (30-80 lines) — only the module you need
3. Done. ~130 lines vs ~6500 in classic GRACE.

**NEVER** read monolithic `knowledge-graph.xml`, `development-plan.xml`, or `verification-plan.xml` — they don't exist in MyGRACE.

## Six Core Principles
1. **Never Write Code Without a Contract** — MODULE_CONTRACT before code
2. **Semantic Markup Is Not Comments** — START_BLOCK/END_BLOCK are navigation anchors
3. **Knowledge Graph Is Always Current** — graph-index.xml never drifts
4. **Top-Down Synthesis** — Requirements → Technology → Plan → Verification → Contracts → Code
5. **Verification Is Architecture** — tests, traces, log markers are part of the blueprint
6. **Governed Autonomy (PCAM)** — Purpose, Constraints, Autonomy, Metrics

## Project Structure
```
docs/
  graph-index.xml              ← ALWAYS read first (≤100 lines)
  plan-index.xml               ← Phase index (≤50 lines)
  verification-index.xml       ← Verification index (≤80 lines)
  operational-packets.xml
  modules/                     ← Per-module files (M-XXX.xml)
  plans/                       ← Per-phase files (Phase-N.xml)
  verification/                ← Per-verification files (V-M-XXX.xml)
  archive/
```

## Key Artifacts
- MODULE_CONTRACT in each file — WHAT each module does
- START_BLOCK / END_BLOCK — semantic navigation anchors
- CHANGE_SUMMARY — change tracking
- Per-module files (docs/modules/M-XXX.xml) — 30-80 lines each
- Per-phase files (docs/plans/Phase-N.xml) — 50-200 lines each
- Per-verification files (docs/verification/V-M-XXX.xml) — 20-60 lines each

